----- RATIONALE (honesty covenant) -----
capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 present (Compose BOM via libs catalog, material3); Kotlin/Compose plugins applied; JDK 21 runner, Android SDK 36 (ANDROID_HOME set). assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest + ktlintCheck + detekt all green => capability satisfied, NOT blocked.
module-path: prompt gate says :app:assembleRelease, but settings.gradle.kts maps app/ -> :android (there is no :app project). Ran :android:* (the real path every P3/A* gate uses); documented above. No scope narrowing.
data: view performs NO HTTP. ServiceHealthSectionSource is the P1/S8 seam; the ViewModel projects Resource<JsonElement> -> ServiceHealthData -> UiState via BaseFeedViewModel.asUiState (ADR-013 cache-then-network). The surface binds the RAW /telemetry payload, NOT the shared TelemetryStore.mqttStatus(): that store normalizes /telemetry to the lossy useMQTTStatus shape (connected/broker/uptime/vehicles/topics) which DROPS enabled, mode, and aggregate_stats. Binding to it would silently narrow parity (3 missing MetricCards + the Enabled badge), so this surface owns the raw-JSON port + full projection (the FleetApiSection precedent for dev-tools endpoints; the HealthProbesSection precedent for raw-JSON projection). A host supplies the production adapter over the shared resilient ApiHttpClient feed.
states: every P3 state renders -> loading (Skeleton block + a11y label, web isLoading), content (4 MetricCards + sortable/paginated vehicles DataTable, web success), empty (payload not an object => friendly EmptyState "No telemetry data available", never a blank box, web !data), error (QueryError + retry, web error), and stale + offline (cached metrics + table kept visible + a freshness chip in the header + one auto-refresh, ADR-013, mirroring the web 2s refetch). No fabricated state, no red-as-green.
i18n: every displayed string resolves through the Android resource facade (P1/S10) via resolveServiceHealthText("translation_<sanitized-key>"), reproducing react-i18next's natural-key fallback 1:1. Catalog-backed keys (Mode, Status, Signals, Latency, Streaming, Idle, VIN, streaming + the pagination labels) localize; the web's untranslated natural keys (Service Health, Fleet Telemetry streaming status, Enabled, Disabled, Vehicles Connected, Total Signals, Avg Signals/s, Signals/s, Last Received, the empty hints) fall back to the key text exactly as the web t() does. Raw mode + per-vehicle timestamps are data shown verbatim (web {data.mode}/formatDateTime), not UI copy. NOTE: catalog entries live in P1/S10 strings.xml, outside this artifact's allowed-files scope, so absent keys use the documented fallback (identical on-screen text to web).
a11y: header is one merged Button node carrying expand/collapse action label + aria-expanded state description; QueryError retry, the loading region (contentDescription), and the freshness chip all expose accessible names; the VIN/status/numeric table cells and metric tiles carry their own text. API 26+ target. Reduced motion honored via FadeIn / rememberMotionDurationMs.
tests: adapter unit test (ServiceHealthProjectionTest, 14 tests) + ViewModel state test (ServiceHealthSectionViewModelTest, 8 tests) run in the JVM testReleaseUnitTest gate (22 green, 0 failures/errors/skipped). Per-state UI + a11y test (ServiceHealthSectionUiTest, androidTest) uses only resolvable finders (assertIsDisplayed / onNodeWithText / onNodeWithContentDescription / performClick); the repo's androidTest set is pre-existingly non-compiling on unrelated widget tests, which is why the gate runs JVM unit tests not connectedAndroidTest, and running the instrumented suite additionally needs a device/emulator (unavailable here) — same disposition as the sibling HealthProbesSection log.
placeholder: PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0. The one PLACEHOLDER_ALLOWED is value.toDouble() in formatCount (the 'toDo' substring trips the case-insensitive TODO pattern) — a numeric conversion, marked // parity:allow with a reason, identical to the sibling HealthProbesSectionModel.
footprint: com/teslasync/feature-views/ServiceHealthSection/{ServiceHealthSection,ServiceHealthSectionModel,ServiceHealthSectionSource,ServiceHealthSectionViewModel}.kt + the two test packages (featureviews/servicehealth in test + androidTest) + this log. Satellite + Zap glyphs reuse MapsGlyphs.Satellite / DataDisplayGlyphs.Bolt; Radio + TrendingUp are local lucide-style vectors (shared layer carries no match), mirroring HealthProbesSection's local HeartPulse.

